Done. Here's what I shipped:

### Summary

**Real-time bash output streaming via on_progress** — closes gap #1 vs Claude Code.

**What changed in src/tools.rs:**

1. Reader loop now tracks line source: The tokio::select! returns (String, bool) tuples where the bool indicates stderr origin, instead of just the line string.

2. Per-line progress emission: After each line is accumulated, ctx.on_progress() is called with the line text. Stdout lines are emitted as-is; stderr lines get a `stderr:  prefix. This produces AgentEvent::ProgressMessage` events that the prompt.rs renderer already handles — printing each as dim text immediately.

3. Interactive-only gating: A new progress_requires_tty: bool field (defaults true) ensures progress emission only happens when stderr is a terminal. In piped mode, no streaming output interferes with structured output. Tests set this to false to verify progress behavior in CI.

4. Backward compatibility preserved: The existing on_update periodic snapshots, the final ToolResult format, the update interval/lines-per-update settings — all unchanged.

**5 new tests:**
• test_streaming_bash_progress_emits_each_line — verifies each stdout line arrives via on_progress
• test_streaming_bash_progress_stderr_prefix — verifies stderr lines get stderr:  prefix, stdout lines don't
• `test_streaming_bash_progress_complete_output_unchanged` — verifies final result still has full buffered output
• `test_streaming_bash_progress_with_timeout` — verifies timeout still works with progress active
• test_streaming_bash_progress_with_cancellation — verifies cancellation still works with progress active

